# Rank Math API Manager Plugin - Development Rules

## 🚫 Git Operations

- **NEVER commit and push without explicit user consent**
- Always ask for permission before any git operations
- Provide clear summaries of changes before committing
- Use descriptive commit messages following conventional commits

## 🎯 WordPress Coding Standards

- Follow [WordPress Coding Standards](https://developer.wordpress.org/coding-standards/wordpress-coding-standards/)
- Use WordPress naming conventions (snake_case for functions, camelCase for variables)
- Follow PSR-12 for PHP code formatting
- Use WordPress file structure and organization
- Implement proper error handling with WordPress functions

## 🔧 WordPress Plugin Development Best Practices

- Use the WordPress Plugin API for all functionality
- Implement proper plugin activation/deactivation hooks
- Use WordPress hooks and filters for extensibility
- Follow WordPress plugin header standards
- Implement proper uninstall procedures
- Use WordPress constants and functions instead of hardcoded values

## 🛡️ Security Requirements

- **ALWAYS implement nonce verification** for forms and AJAX requests
- Use WordPress sanitization functions:
  - `sanitize_text_field()` for text inputs
  - `sanitize_textarea_field()` for textarea content
  - `esc_url_raw()` for URLs
  - `wp_kses_post()` for HTML content
  - `intval()` for numeric values
- Implement proper capability checks (`current_user_can()`)
- Validate and escape all output using `esc_html()`, `esc_attr()`, `esc_url()`
- Use prepared statements for database queries
- Implement rate limiting for API endpoints
- Validate file uploads and file types
- Use WordPress nonces for CSRF protection

## 📜 Script and Style Management

- **ALWAYS use `wp_enqueue_script()` and `wp_enqueue_style()`**
- Never include scripts/styles directly in HTML
- Use proper dependencies and versioning
- Implement conditional loading based on context
- Use WordPress asset minification when possible
- Follow WordPress script/style naming conventions

## 🏗️ WordPress Plugin API Usage

- Leverage WordPress Plugin API for extending functionality
- Use hooks and filters for modularity and scalability
- Implement proper action and filter priorities
- Use WordPress plugin lifecycle hooks appropriately
- Create reusable functions and classes
- Implement proper error handling and logging

## 📝 Custom Post Types and Taxonomies

- Use custom post types when extending WordPress functionality
- Implement proper taxonomy relationships
- Use WordPress register functions (`register_post_type()`, `register_taxonomy()`)
- Follow WordPress naming conventions for CPTs and taxonomies
- Implement proper capabilities and permissions
- Use WordPress meta boxes and custom fields appropriately

## 🔍 Code Quality Standards

- Write self-documenting code with clear variable and function names
- Use meaningful comments for complex logic
- Implement proper error handling and logging
- Write unit tests for critical functionality
- Use WordPress debugging functions (`WP_DEBUG`, `error_log()`)
- Follow DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principles
- Implement proper separation of concerns

## 🚀 Performance Optimization

- Use WordPress caching mechanisms
- Optimize database queries with proper indexing
- Implement lazy loading where appropriate
- Use WordPress transients for temporary data
- Minimize HTTP requests
- Optimize asset loading and delivery
- Use WordPress object caching when available

## 🔧 API Development Standards

- Follow REST API best practices
- Implement proper HTTP status codes
- Use WordPress REST API framework when possible
- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Use WordPress REST API endpoints structure
- Implement proper error responses
- Use WordPress REST API validation

## 📚 Documentation Requirements

- Document all public functions and classes
- Use PHPDoc comments for all functions
- Maintain up-to-date README and changelog
- Document API endpoints and parameters
- Include usage examples in documentation
- Document security considerations
- Maintain inline code comments for complex logic

## 🧪 Testing Requirements

- Write unit tests for critical functionality
- Test with WordPress Plugin Check (PCP)
- Test compatibility with different WordPress versions
- Test with different PHP versions
- Test with various server configurations
- Implement integration tests for API endpoints
- Test security measures and validation

## 🔄 Version Control

- Use semantic versioning (semver.org)
- Maintain detailed changelog entries
- Use feature branches for development
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Review code before merging
- Tag releases appropriately
- Maintain clean git history

## 🛠️ Development Environment

- Use WordPress development best practices
- Implement proper debugging tools
- Use WordPress coding standards tools
- Maintain consistent code formatting
- Use version control for all changes
- Implement proper backup strategies
- Test in staging environment before production

## 📋 Plugin-Specific Rules

- Always check for Rank Math SEO plugin dependency
- Implement proper error handling for missing dependencies
- Use WordPress REST API for all external communications
- Implement proper logging for API operations
- Validate all input data before processing
- Use WordPress nonces for all form submissions
